    }
  >
    <Text
      style={
        {
          "fontSize": 24,
          "fontWeight": 700,
          "marginTop": 30,
        }
      }
    >
      <Text
        style={
          [
            {},
            {},
          ]
        }
      >
        <Text>
          Dynamic troubles
        </Text>
      </Text>
    </Text>
  </View>
  <View
    style={
      {
        "marginVertical": 5,
      }
    }
  >
    <Text
      style={
        [
          {},
          {},
        ]
      }
    >
      <Text
        style={
          [
            {},
            {},
          ]
        }
      >
        <Text>
          We've tackled blocks and styles, but there is still one more layer to all of this. The way information is stored in blocks is quite convoluted. We have 2 main types of blocks - Static and Dynamic.
        </Text>
      </Text>
    </Text>
  </View>
  <View
    style={
      {
        "marginVertical": 5,
      }
    }
  >
    <Text
      style={
        [
          {},
          {},
        ]
      }
    >
      <Text
        style={
          [
            {},
            {},
          ]
        }
      >
        <Text>
          Static blocks are saved as a fixed HTML snippet. There is no additional processing required when serving them to the user. For the structure, they contain all the necessary information to parse them in the app in innerHTML and attrs.
        </Text>
      </Text>
    </Text>
  </View>
  <View
    style={
      {
        "marginVertical": 5,
      }
    }
  >
    <Text
      style={
        [
          {},
          {},
        ]
      }
    >
      <Text
        style={
          [
            {},
            {},
          ]
        }
      >
        <Text>
          Dynamic blocks however are a different breed. They store almost no data in the form of fixed HTML. Instead they are rendered server-side for each request.
        </Text>
      </Text>
    </Text>
  </View>
  <View
    style={
      {
        "marginVertical": 5,
      }
    }
  >
