  >
    <Text
      style={
        {
          "fontSize": 24,
          "fontWeight": 700,
          "marginTop": 30,
        }
      }
    >
      <Text
        style={
          [
            {},
            {},
          ]
        }
      >
        <Text>
          The remedy
        </Text>
      </Text>
    </Text>
  </View>
  <View
    style={
      {
        "marginVertical": 5,
      }
    }
  >
    <Text
      style={
        [
          {},
          {},
        ]
      }
    >
      <Text
        style={
          [
            {},
            {},
          ]
        }
      >
        <Text>
          The only thing that comes to mind in situations like these is tokenization. What if we could artificially close the existing 
        </Text>
        <Text
          style={
            {
              "fontWeight": 700,
            }
          }
        >
          <Text
            style={
              {
                "fontFamily": "Menlo",
              }
            }
          >
            <Text>
              Text
            </Text>
          </Text>
        </Text>
        <Text>
           tags before opening an 
        </Text>
        <Text
          style={
            {
              "fontWeight": 700,
            }
          }
        >
          <Text
            style={
              {
                "fontFamily": "Menlo",
              }
            }
          >
            <Text>
              Image
            </Text>
          </Text>
        </Text>
        <Text>
          ? Then even if we got the same input structure as above, we would end up with a different output structure. We would go through the HTML while keeping "opening" tags on the stack and flushing the content if we encounter 
        </Text>
        <Text
          style={
            {
              "fontWeight": 700,
            }
          }
        >
          <Text
            style={
              {
                "fontFamily": "Menlo",
              }
            }
          >
            <Text>
              Image
            </Text>
          </Text>
        </Text>
        <Text>
           or any other tag we want to "fish out" from 
        </Text>
        <Text
          style={
            {
              "fontWeight": 700,
            }
          }
        >
          <Text
            style={
              {
                "fontFamily": "Menlo",
              }
            }
          >
            <Text>
              Text
            </Text>
          </Text>
        </Text>
        <Text>
          .
        </Text>
      </Text>
    </Text>
  </View>
  <View
    style={
      {
        "marginVertical": 5,
