      <Text
        style={
          [
            {},
            {},
          ]
        }
      >
        <Text>
          This however brings another problem. If we take 
        </Text>
        <Text
          style={
            {
              "fontWeight": 700,
            }
          }
        >
          <Text
            style={
              {
                "fontFamily": "Menlo",
              }
            }
          >
            <Text>
              Image
            </Text>
          </Text>
        </Text>
        <Text>
           out of 
        </Text>
        <Text
          style={
            {
              "fontWeight": 700,
            }
          }
        >
          <Text
            style={
              {
                "fontFamily": "Menlo",
              }
            }
          >
            <Text>
              &lt;a&gt;
            </Text>
          </Text>
        </Text>
        <Text>
          , how are we supposed to keep the functionality of linking? Just use 
        </Text>
        <Text
          style={
            {
              "fontFamily": "Menlo",
            }
          }
        >
          <Text>
            Context
          </Text>
        </Text>
        <Text>
           and consume it in 
        </Text>
        <Text
          style={
            {
              "fontFamily": "Menlo",
            }
          }
        >
          <Text>
            Image
          </Text>
        </Text>
        <Text>
          . Then simply render an alternate version if we are inside 
        </Text>
        <Text
          style={
            {
              "fontFamily": "Menlo",
            }
          }
        >
          <Text>
            &lt;a&gt;
          </Text>
        </Text>
        <Text>
          .
        </Text>
